            <div xml:id="d476">

                <pb facs="0483" n="479" xml:id="pg479"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.93 Manchuria/183: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-08-12T10:00:00+03:00">August 12, 1938—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 12—6:54 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>252, My 250, August 10 [<hi rendition="#italic">11</hi>], 2 p.m.<anchor n="29"
                        xml:id="d476-f1"/> Tass communiqué issued last night states that as agreed
                    between the Soviet Union and Japan on August 10 hostilities in the zone of Lake
                    Khasan ceased on August 11 at 13:30 local time. The first meeting of military
                    representatives of both sides for the purpose of fixation of the position of
                    troops took place south of Height Zaozernaya (Changkufeng) on the evening of
                    August 11. The next meeting is scheduled for 12 noon August 12.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
